<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.7.1: Comparing Graphs of Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01848</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.7.1: Comparing Graphs of Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>de1086c3-a18e-4663-8024-93eed1f2033b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Which one doesn’t belong?</para>
          <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
            <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
              <para>Graph A</para>
              <para>
                <figure>
                  <media alt="Graph of a line, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis from negative 2 to 2 by 1’s. Vertical axis from negative 2 to 6 by ones. Line passes through negative 2 comma 2, 0 comma 2, and 2 comma 2.&quot; height=&quot;200">
                    <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_09_02_01.svg"/>
                  </media>
                </figure>
              </para>
            </div>
            <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
              <para>Graph B</para>
              <para>
                <figure>
                  <media alt="Graph of a line, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis from negative 2 to 2 by 1’s. Vertical axis from negative 2 to 6 by ones. Line passes through negative 1 comma negative 2, 0 comma 2, and 1 comma 6.&quot; height=&quot;200">
                    <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_09_02_02.svg"/>
                  </media>
                </figure>
              </para>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
            <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
              <para>Graph C</para>
              <para>
                <figure>
                  <media alt="Graph of 13 data points.">
                    <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_09_02_03.svg"/>
                  </media>
                </figure>
              </para>
            </div>
            <div class="os-raise-mx-auto">
              <para>Graph D</para>
              <para>
                <figure>
                  <media alt="Graph of curved line, origin O, with grid. Horizontal axis from negative 2 to 2 by 1’s. Vertical axis from negative 2 to 6 by 1’s. Line passes through negative 1 comma point 5, 0 comma 3 point 5, 1 comma 7.&quot; height=&quot;200">
                    <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_09_02_04.svg"/>
                  </media>
                </figure>
              </para>
            </div>
          </div>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Graph A is the only graph where the \(y\)-values don’t change.</para>
          <para>Graph B is the only graph where the \(y\)-value increases by a constant rate.</para>
          <para>Graph C is the only graph that is not continuous.</para>
          <para>Graph D is the only graph that does not intersect the \(y\)-axis at \(2\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
